  "title": "Volatility Ranking",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "27482200-1fd5-4fc8-9871-fda301c8beb1",
      "question": "Among the 50 most liquid US stocks, which five had the highest and which five the lowest daily volatility over the 60 trading sessions ending March 12, 2026, and what were their returns over those sessions?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T18:53:22.642489Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T18:53:38.999175Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Among the 50 most liquid US stocks over the 60 trading sessions ending **March 12, 2026**:\n\n### Highest daily volatility (standard deviation of daily returns)\n\n| Rank | Ticker | Daily volatility | 60-session return |\n|------|--------|------------------|-------------------|\n| 1 | CRWV | 6.92% | +1.57% |\n| 2 | CRCL | 6.81% | +36.77% |\n| 3 | BMNR | 6.18% | –40.94% |\n| 4 | APP | 6.07% | –33.08% |\n| 5 | COIN | 5.26% | –27.95% |\n\n### Lowest daily volatility\n\n| Rank | Ticker | Daily volatility | 60-session return |\n|------|--------|------------------|-------------------|\n| 1 | KO | 1.02% | +10.11% |\n| 2 | JNJ | 1.03% | +14.11% |\n| 3 | BRK.B | 1.12% | –1.55% |\n| 4 | PG | 1.27% | +5.36% |\n| 5 | COST | 1.31% | +13.44% |\n\nVolatility is the standard deviation of daily returns over the window. Returns run from the close before the first session to the close of the last session (March 12, 2026). [1][2]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:f705413f7123ea5d197892ed19c76e95f16be79d6ee6e544ca8c974f0479e96b`\n- [2] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:6ad4594b5f0020dbece00f4bdcbd5bea6b5a57ddfd8975b67cc94ec4aaeeb6b5`",
